<section class="workspace-page bunker-workspace" data-bunker-root aria-labelledby="bunker-heading">
  <div class="workspace-heading bunker-heading">
    <div><p class="bunker-eyebrow">NODE ADMINISTRATION / NOSTR</p><h1 id="bunker-heading">Bunker</h1>
      </div>
  </div>
  <section class="bunker-live" aria-label="Current health">
    <div><strong id="bunker-live-status" role="status">Loading…</strong><small id="bunker-live-time">Current health</small></div>
    <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-action="health">Check health</button>
  </section>
  <section class="workspace-card bunker-card bunker-next-card" id="bunker-next-card" aria-labelledby="bunker-next-title">
    <div class="bunker-next-meta">
      <p class="bunker-eyebrow" id="bunker-next-phase">Handover</p>
      <span class="bunker-badge" id="bunker-next-status">Loading</span>
    </div>
    <p class="bunker-next-owner"><strong id="bunker-next-owner">You</strong></p>
    <h2 id="bunker-next-title" tabindex="-1">Handover</h2>
    <p id="bunker-next-description">Loading progress…</p>
    <div class="bunker-actions bunker-next-actions">
      <button type="button" class="workspace-button bunker-primary" id="bunker-next-action" disabled>Loading…</button>
      <button type="button" class="workspace-button" id="bunker-next-alternate" hidden>Continue</button>
    </div>
    <details id="bunker-inline-commands" hidden><summary>View commands</summary>
      <p>Run in Bash with AWS CLI v2, jq and Python 3. Use an authorised administrator profile.</p>
      <pre class="bunker-cli"><code>export BUNKER_ADMIN_PROFILE='your-admin-profile'</code></pre>
      <pre class="bunker-cli"><code id="bunker-inline-code"></code></pre>
    </details>
    <p class="bunker-next-footer"><a id="bunker-next-help" href="#bunker-closing-guide" data-bunker-go hidden>Help</a> · <a href="#bunker-acceptance-guide" data-bunker-go>Sign-off</a>
      <small id="bunker-next-progress" aria-live="polite" hidden></small></p>
  </section>
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card" id="bunker-signoff-panel" hidden><h2 id="bunker-acceptance-guide" tabindex="-1">Sign off</h2>
      <p>Attach the four review references. Submit to refresh health and record sign-off.</p>
      <form id="bunker-acceptance">
        <label>Effective IAM permissions reviewed<input name="iam_reviewed" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-iam-help" placeholder="CHG-2041/iam-review"></label>
        <p id="bunker-iam-help" class="bunker-field-help">IAM review: runtime role, secret policy, KMS and applicable permission limits. Reference the reviewed record.</p>
        <label>Temporary administrator access removed<input name="temporary_admin_removed" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-admin-help" placeholder="CHG-2041/admin-removal"></label>
        <p id="bunker-admin-help" class="bunker-field-help">Reference removal of temporary grants, credentials and sessions. Keep the runtime role.</p>
        <h3 id="bunker-external-guide" tabindex="-1">Independent external-client acceptance</h3>
        <label>External client accepted<input name="external_client_accepted" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-external-help" placeholder="UAT-2041/external-client"></label>
        <p id="bunker-external-help" class="bunker-field-help">Reference the independent client test: client key, relay, event ID, verified signature and owner acceptance.</p>
        <h3 id="bunker-backup-guide" tabindex="-1">Retained backup and recovery custodian</h3>
        <label>Recovery custodian and retained backup confirmed<input name="recovery_custodian_confirmed" required minlength="8" maxlength="256" aria-describedby="bunker-backup-help" placeholder="OPS-2041/recovery-custody"></label>
        <p id="bunker-backup-help" class="bunker-field-help">Reference the retained encrypted backup, integrity check, recovery runbook and named custodian. Test copies are deleted.</p>
        <p>Sign-off refreshes health and checks that the reviewed report is unchanged.</p>
        <button type="submit" class="workspace-button bunker-primary" id="bunker-accept">Sign off</button>
      </form>
      <p id="bunker-acceptance-state"></p>
      <p>Keep the report and supporting records in the handover ticket.</p>
      <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-export>Export handover evidence</button>
    </article>
  <p id="bunker-message" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading recorded evidence…</p>
  <details id="bunker-details" class="bunker-details">
    <summary>Advanced details</summary>
    <div class="bunker-actions bunker-detail-actions"><button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-action="health">Check health</button>
      <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-action="verify">Verify signing</button></div>
  <div class="bunker-summary" id="bunker-summary" aria-label="Verification summary"></div>
  <nav class="bunker-tabs" aria-label="Bunker views">
    <button type="button" data-bunker-tab="overview" aria-pressed="true">Overview</button>
    <button type="button" data-bunker-tab="setup" aria-pressed="false">Setup</button>
    <button type="button" data-bunker-tab="evidence" aria-pressed="false">Evidence</button>
    <button type="button" data-bunker-tab="recovery" aria-pressed="false">Recovery &amp; handover</button>
  </nav>
  <section data-bunker-pane="overview">
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card"><h2 id="bunker-health-guide" tabindex="-1">Health checks</h2>
      <p>Run a health check. Failed controls show the next action.</p>
      <div class="bunker-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Result</th><th>Next action</th></tr></thead><tbody id="bunker-checks"></tbody></table></div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section data-bunker-pane="setup" hidden>
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card"><h2 id="bunker-setup-guide" tabindex="-1">Settings</h2>
      <p>Apply configuration changes through your release process.</p>
      <dl id="bunker-setup" class="bunker-config"></dl>
      <h3 id="bunker-identity-guide" tabindex="-1">Deployment and signing identity</h3>
      <p>Compare the signing key with your approved record. Resolve mismatches before continuing.</p>
      <h3 id="bunker-custody-guide" tabindex="-1">AWS custody and runtime access</h3>
      <p>Use a separate AWS administrator profile. The bunker runtime stays read-only.</p>
      <pre class="bunker-cli"><code>export BUNKER_ADMIN_PROFILE='your-admin-profile'</code></pre>
      <details><summary>Inspect AWS identity, secret versions and role policies</summary>
        <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-copy="inspect" disabled>Copy inspection commands</button>
        <pre class="bunker-cli"><code id="bunker-cli-inspect">Loading AWS configuration…</code></pre>
      </details>
      <h3 id="bunker-relay-guide" tabindex="-1">Relays, clients and policy</h3>
      <p>Use 1–6 WSS relays and approved clients. Allow connect, ping, get_public_key and sign_event for kind 30023; keep publishing disabled.</p>
      <h3 id="bunker-files-guide" tabindex="-1">Host files</h3>
      <p>Vault and audit files must be private and owned by the service account. The crypto backend must be executable and not writable by group or others.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section data-bunker-pane="evidence" hidden>
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card"><div class="bunker-row"><h2 id="bunker-signing-guide" tabindex="-1">Signing tests</h2>
      <button type="button" class="workspace-button" id="bunker-export" data-bunker-export>Export evidence</button></div><p>Test every relay and signing policy. Independent client acceptance is separate.</p>
      <div class="bunker-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Relay</th><th>Probe</th><th>Result</th><th>Correlation</th></tr></thead><tbody id="bunker-exchanges"></tbody></table></div>
      <details><summary>Report details</summary><pre id="bunker-report-detail"></pre></details>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section data-bunker-pane="recovery" hidden>
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card"><h2 id="bunker-closing-guide" tabindex="-1">Close the handover</h2>
      <p>All technical checks must pass before sign-off.</p>
      <h3>Closing checklist</h3>
      <p>Only passed checks count toward completion.</p>
      <div class="bunker-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Result</th><th>Next action</th></tr></thead><tbody id="bunker-closing-checks"></tbody></table></div></article>
    <article class="workspace-card bunker-card"><h2>Manual tests</h2>
      <div class="bunker-maintenance">
        <div><h3 id="bunker-pending-guide" tabindex="-1">Prepare version</h3>
      <p>AWS admin: prepare the version, then run the test below. Copying commands does not execute them.</p>
          <details><summary>AWS CLI — prepare AWSPENDING</summary>
            <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-copy="pending" disabled>Copy prepare commands</button>
            <pre class="bunker-cli"><code id="bunker-cli-pending">Loading AWS configuration…</code></pre>
          </details>
          <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-action="pending">Check pending version</button><p class="bunker-critical">After promotion, continue to recovery. Do not repeat the pending test.</p>
        </div>
        <div><h3 id="bunker-restore-guide" tabindex="-1">Activate and recover</h3>
      <p>AWS admin: promote the tested version. Then test recovery below.</p>
          <details><summary>AWS CLI — promote the tested version</summary>
            <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-copy="promote" disabled>Copy promotion commands</button>
            <pre class="bunker-cli"><code id="bunker-cli-promote">Complete the pending rehearsal first.</code></pre>
          </details>
          <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-action="recovery">Verify current version &amp; restore</button><p>Tests an isolated restore. Keep a separate retained backup.</p>
        </div>
        <div><h3 id="bunker-restart-guide" tabindex="-1">Restart test</h3>
      <p>Remove temporary admin access first. Restart briefly interrupts signing and runs fresh signing tests.</p>
          <button type="button" class="workspace-button" data-bunker-action="restart">Restart &amp; verify</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="bunker-maintenance-results"></div>
      <h3 id="bunker-versions-guide" tabindex="-1">Recorded version IDs</h3>
      <p>Recorded version IDs; compare with AWS if a test fails.</p>
      <dl id="bunker-version-evidence" class="bunker-config"></dl>
    </article>

  </section>
  </details>
  <dialog id="bunker-confirm"><form method="dialog"><h2 id="bunker-confirm-title">Confirm maintenance</h2>
    <p id="bunker-confirm-text"></p><div class="bunker-actions"><button value="cancel" class="workspace-button">Cancel</button><button value="proceed" class="workspace-button bunker-primary">Proceed</button></div>
  </form></dialog>
</section>
